        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1001">

                <pb facs="0772" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 853.00/191.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-06-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of Department’s June 6. It is
                    probable that Constituent Assembly will definitely proclaim the Republic on 22d
                    instant but several weeks may elapse before a constitution is decided upon and
                    President chosen. Am I to understand the proclamation of the Republic by the
                    Assembly to mean definite and final action?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lorillard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
